@startuml wallbreaker-pigeonhole
' WallBreaker beats the "wall effect" for large k via the pigeonhole principle.
' Color legend:
'   teal   = input pattern        amber  = split step
'   green  = error-free piece / accepted candidate
'   red    = piece that absorbed an edit
'   purple = bidirectional verification
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 12
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title WallBreaker — pigeonhole filtering   (shown: <latex>k = 2</latex> ⇒ <latex>k+1 = 3</latex> pieces)

rectangle "Pattern  P   (<latex>\vert P\vert = m</latex>)" as P #B2EBF2

together {
  rectangle "P₁\n(exact)" as p1 #C8E6C9
  rectangle "P₂\n(1 edit)" as p2 #FFCDD2
  rectangle "P₃\n(exact)" as p3 #C8E6C9
}
note right of p3
  With <latex>\le k</latex> edits spread across k+1 disjoint pieces,
  by the pigeonhole principle at least one piece (here P₁, P₃)
  must be error-free.
end note

rectangle "Locate the error-free piece exactly in the SCDAWG\n<latex>\mathcal{O}(\vert P_{i}\vert)</latex> — no wall, no prefix blow-up" as M #C8E6C9
rectangle "Extend the match bidirectionally\n(left ← and → right) within the remaining edit budget" as E #E1BEE7
rectangle "Verify total edits <latex>\le k</latex>\n→ candidate (term, distance)" as V #C8E6C9

P -[#00838F]down-> p2 : "split into k+1 pieces"
p1 -[hidden]right- p2
p2 -[hidden]right- p3
p2 -[#EF6C00]down-> M
M -[#6A1B9A]down-> E
E -[#2E7D32]down-> V
@enduml
